"content_id": "14403",
"reference_id": 13571,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:1–4",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001001-64001004",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>The apostle John begins his letter with a common greeting. It includes:</p><ul><li><p>identifying himself and the person he is writing to,</p></li><li><p>using a friendly greeting, such as <em>beloved</em>,</p></li><li><p>offering wishes for the person&apos;s well-being, and</p></li><li><p> expressing thanks for their friendship.</p></li></ul>",
