{
"content_id": "14415",
"reference_id": 13583,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:6",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001006",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>The church mentioned here was probably in Ephesus, where John was likely staying. Ephesus was an important port city in the province of Asia and was the fourth-largest city in the Roman Empire. It later became an important center for the Christian community (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"44018019\" data-end-ref=\"44019041\">Acts 18:19–19:41</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"54001003\" data-end-ref=\"54001003\">1&nbsp;Timothy 1:3</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"60001001\" data-end-ref=\"60001001\">1&nbsp;Peter 1:1</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"66002001\" data-end-ref=\"66002007\">Revelation 2:1–7</data>).</p>",
"associations": {
