{
"content_id": "14418",
"reference_id": 13586,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:9",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001009",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p><span><em>I have written to the church about this</em>: </span>This could refer to 1 John or to a letter that is now lost.</p></li><li><p>Diotrephes was proud and thought himself important. He was motivated by selfish ambition (see <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"54003006\" data-end-ref=\"54003006\">1 Timothy 3:6</data>).</p></li><li><p><span><em>will not accept our instruction</em>: </span>This disagreement was a major issue that John addressed in 1 John (see, for example, <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"62002019\" data-end-ref=\"62002019\">1 John 2:19</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"62004005\" data-end-ref=\"62004006\">4:5–6</data>). Diotrephes rejected the teachers sent by John and removed any church members who accepted them. He wanted to lead the local church without answering to any outside authority.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "64001009",
"start_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:9",
"end_ref": "64001009",
"end_ref_usfm": "3JN 1:9"
}
],
