{
"content_id": "14405",
"reference_id": 13573,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "3 John 1:12",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "64001012",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Demetrius was the opposite of Diotrephes. Demetrius was a clear example of a person who knows the truth and lives according to it (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"64001003\" data-end-ref=\"64001003\">1:3</data>). His name appears at the end of the letter. This suggests that he was the person who carried John’s letter to Gaius (compare <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"51004007\" data-end-ref=\"51004009\">Colossians 4:7–9</data>; <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"60005012\" data-end-ref=\"60005012\">1&nbsp;Peter 5:12</data>).</p></li><li><p><span><em>you know that our testimony is true</em></span>: John wanted to protect his honor as a trustworthy elder for these churches. He did not want Diotrephes or other false teachers to challenge or replace his leadership.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
